<!--
  The solution Stryker builds for a mutation run. Stryker does not build only the project
  under mutation and its test project. It discovers a solution and runs
  `dotnet build <solution>` over all of it. Pointed at XLibur.slnx that is sixteen projects
  at up to three target frameworks each: the benchmarks, the examples, XLibur.Report and
  six test projects that no mutation run touches.

  This holds the actual closure of XLibur.Tests, which is the library under mutation, the
  test project, and the two projects XLibur.Tests references (both of which reference only
  XLibur).

  Keep in step with the ProjectReference list in XLibur.Tests/XLibur.Tests.csproj. A project
  added there and forgotten here fails the mutation build, not the normal one.
-->
<Solution>
  <Project Path="XLibur/XLibur.csproj" />
  <Project Path="XLibur.Tests/XLibur.Tests.csproj" />
  <Project Path="XLibur.Examples/XLibur.Examples.csproj" />
  <Project Path="XLibur.Fonts.SixLabors.V1/XLibur.Fonts.SixLabors.V1.csproj" />
</Solution>
